      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T14:18:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These are `unsafe` because you\u0027re telling Rust to track ownership of memory it has not allocated. So safety comes down to whether this is a unique reference or not, otherwise the borrow checked is useless. You can claim it is safe but you should first check that the slices don\u0027t overlap with pvmfw memory and with each other.",
