      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right; I wanted to validate them in `main_wrapper` once we have a logger but I see your point and how I confused security (\"we don\u0027t trust the inputs\") and safety (\"the compiler makes correct assumptions\").\n\nFor now, I\u0027ll pass the inputs to `main_wrapper`, record that validation is a `TODO` and argue that the `SAFETY` comes from `crosvm` not being buggy (which is enough for `pvmfw` in its current state). Validation will be added once we start actually using the inputs, at which point we\u0027ll have logging in `main_wrapper`.",
